&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab features must ship successfully across four distinct deployment platforms—Self-Managed, Dedicated, Dedicated for Government, and GitLab.com. Today, developers routinely discover platform compatibility issues late in development, triggering costly rework, delays, and emergency escalations. The Platform Readiness team is building an internal developer tooling capability that embeds platform readiness intelligence directly into GitLab&#39;s software development lifecycle to solve this problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Backend Engineer on the newly established Platform Readiness team, you&#39;ll architect and evolve the systems that enable features to ship successfully across all platforms by automating the evaluation of platform readiness requirements and surfacing risks early. You&#39;ll be a technical anchor for the team, driving the evolution of platform readiness from manual, ad-hoc assessments toward intelligent, agentic automation. Your work will directly impact GitLab&#39;s ability to ship features faster while dramatically reducing the risk of platform-readiness gaps and the operational burden of cross-platform validation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll receive onboarding and technical guidance from other engineers and team leadership as you establish the technical direction for the Platform Readiness team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to the Platform Readiness team&#39;s agentic workflows&lt;/strong&gt; on the Duo Agent Platform: design, implement, and evolve the Core Agentic Workflow (currently published to the AI Catalog as a DAP flow) and the Requirements Agent, enabling automated evaluation of platform readiness assessments against platform requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evolve the platform requirements knowledge base&lt;/strong&gt;: contribute to schema design, validation tooling, and CI systems that power the agentic workflow; ensure the schema captures the full scope of platform readiness concerns across all four platforms and domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build integration surfaces&lt;/strong&gt; that enable feature teams to engage the Platform Readiness team where they already work: issues, merge requests, design documents, and CI/CD pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with platform teams&lt;/strong&gt; (Infrastructure, Security, Data) to translate their expertise into structured platform requirements, domain skills, and validation logic without requiring specific domain knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to the quality control feedback loop&lt;/strong&gt;: design systems that surface assessment errors, missed gaps, and content drift back to the governance loop for continuous improvement; measure and improve assessment accuracy and guidance relevance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentor other engineers&lt;/strong&gt; on the team in agentic-workflow standards, prompt discipline, evaluation methodology, and the principles of human-AI collaboration in platform readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to technical documentation and architectural decision records&lt;/strong&gt; that document the Platform Readiness team&#39;s technical evolution and rationale for key design choices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Required Experience &amp;amp; Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years of software engineering experience&lt;/strong&gt; with at least 2+ years in backend, platform, or developer-facing tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong proficiency in TypeScript/Node, Python, or Golang&lt;/strong&gt; (Ruby a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience shipping developer-facing tooling&lt;/strong&gt; where the primary user is another engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understanding of GitLab-style development workflows&lt;/strong&gt; (issues, epics, merge requests, CI/CD, code review) as first-class artifacts that automation can read and reason about&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ability to work in cross-functional environments&lt;/strong&gt; across multiple platform teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with structured content systems, schemas, or validation tooling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Highly Valued Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with AI/agentic systems&lt;/strong&gt; (DAP, ADK, LangGraph, or similar) OR demonstrated ability to reason rigorously about the boundary between what AI should decide and what humans must own&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience integrating with LLM APIs&lt;/strong&gt; and reasoning about cost, latency, evaluation, and failure modes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background in developer experience or platform engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with governance patterns&lt;/strong&gt; for shared standards and cross-org decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open source contribution history&lt;/strong&gt; in platform, developer experience, or AI infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PostgreSQL or other relational database experience&lt;/strong&gt; at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Makes You Stand Out (Strong Plus)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve &lt;strong&gt;shipped agentic workflows in production&lt;/strong&gt; and dealt with the operational complexities of AI-driven automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have &lt;strong&gt;experience designing schema-driven content systems&lt;/strong&gt; with non-engineer authors and evolving them as requirements change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve &lt;strong&gt;built developer platform teams at scale&lt;/strong&gt; and understand the dynamics of enabling other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have &lt;strong&gt;observability and monitoring experience for AI systems&lt;/strong&gt;, including evaluation metrics, cost tracking, and failure analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can &lt;strong&gt;explain complex concepts&lt;/strong&gt; (agentic workflows, platform readiness, governance) clearly to platform teams, feature teams, product managers, and executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Platform Readiness team is part of GitLab Developer Experience, building internal developer tooling capability for platform readiness across GitLab&#39;s four deployment targets: Self-Managed, Dedicated, Dedicated for Government, and GitLab.com. We partner with platform teams, feature teams, and product management to ensure every feature is evaluated against platform readiness requirements before it ships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current challenges we&#39;re tackling:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Moving from manual coordination to embedded automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Transitioning from manual, ad-hoc platform readiness assessments to automated, agentic evaluation while maintaining human oversight and trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building a structured, machine-readable requirements body:&lt;/strong&gt; Evolving the platform requirements schema to capture the full scope of platform readiness concerns across all domains and platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Making platform readiness native to the tools feature teams already use:&lt;/strong&gt; Enabling platform teams to contribute domain expertise and validation logic without requiring deep Platform Readiness infrastructure knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Building the measurement systems to know we&#39;re working:&lt;/strong&gt; Creating observability and evaluation frameworks that give us confidence in agentic-workflow decisions and surface failures early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team structure:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be joining a newly established Platform Readiness team that is building the capability to embed platform readiness intelligence into the development lifecycle. As a Senior engineer, you&#39;ll work closely with team leadership to define technical direction while mentoring other engineers on the team. You&#39;ll receive onboarding and technical guidance from other engineers and team leadership on the Platform Readiness team&#39;s architecture and agentic-workflow patterns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
